> if we don't support that on Windows

Indeed, on Windows the implementation of a read lock is the same as a write lock:

````
int CRYPTO_THREAD_read_lock(CRYPTO_RWLOCK *lock)
{
    EnterCriticalSection(lock);
    return 1;
}

int CRYPTO_THREAD_write_lock(CRYPTO_RWLOCK *lock)
{
    EnterCriticalSection(lock);
    return 1;
}
````

It would be great to have support for something better on Windows. What windows versions support SRWLock? We must be careful not to break versions that don't have this support.

What about defining a structure that includes the lock and an indication for read/write?
Something along the lines of:
``` C
struct {
    PSRWLOCK lock;
    int read_write;
};
```
`CRYPTO_THREAD_unlock()` could then check to see what it needs to call.
